Package: tidymarkers
Title: Tidy Design and Quality Control of Genetic Markers
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Daniil", "Ulyanov", email = "uldas1508@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An opinionated, reproducible toolkit for designing and quality
    controlling genetic markers across many chemistries (KASP, CAPS/dCAPS,
    tetra-primer ARMS, HRM, Sanger, SSR, InDel-size, TaqMan/dPCR, SNaPshot,
    LAMP/RPA, CRISPR-Dx).  It is genome-agnostic: supply a reference (FASTA, an
    indexed genome, a DNAStringSet or a Bioconductor BSgenome) and variants (a
    VCF or the tidy variant table), and it designs allele-specific and common
    primers on either strand and scores them.  Thermodynamics come from
    TmCalculator and OligoArrayAux, Taq-aware allelic discrimination from
    DECIPHER, and genome-wide specificity from Biostrings (with an optional
    rBLAST database or an Rsubread FM-index).  Annotation uses VariantAnnotation
    with a transcript database.  A reproducible Arabidopsis thaliana demo (TAIR10
    genome and 1001 Genomes variation) is downloaded from Ensembl Plants into a
    per-user cache on first use; any other reference is supplied directly.
